]},{"s":40126,"e":40320,"k":"block","t":"When this option is enabled, selecting a theme from the Colors tab's color profile dropdown will also apply that theme's font family and size. When disabled, only the theme's colors are applied.","f":[]},{"s":40367,"e":40482,"k":"block","t":"Built-in vs. custom themesKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#built-in-vs-custom-themes\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":40491,"e":40787,"k":"block","t":"korTTY includes a set of built-in color themes (e.g., Default, Dark Mode, Solarized Light). Built-in and custom themes are stored together in a single file, KTPH000. All themes appear in the Colors tab's color profile selector and in connection-specific theme dropdowns.","f":["<code>~/.kortty/themes.xml</code>"]},{"s":40853,"e":40860,"k":"block","t":"Warning","f":[]},{"s":40868,"e":40987,"k":"block","t":"Built-in themes cannot be edited or deleted. To modify a built-in theme, duplicate it first, then edit the custom copy.","f":[]},{"s":41022,"e":41112,"k":"block","t":"Theme previewKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#theme-preview\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":41121,"e":41347,"k":"block","t":"A live theme preview displays the theme's colors. The preview shows six swatches — foreground, background and cursor, plus the AI agent panel's background, run and error colors — so you can evaluate a theme before applying it.","f":[]},{"s":41383,"e":41489,"k":"block","t":"Cross-tab integrationKTPH000","f":["<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#cross-tab-integration\" title=\"Permanent link\">&para;</a>"]},{"s":41504,"e":41668,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Colors tabKTPH001: Choose a theme via the \"Color Profile\" dropdown; if the Themes tab's font option is enabled, the selected theme's font is also applied.","f":["<strong>","</strong>"]},{"s":41678,"e":41859,"k":"block","t":"KTPH000Connection settingsKTPH001: Each individual SSH connection can override the global font and theme via its own settings (accessib